  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/SAPOps"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "sap-shared-acc"}
    }
  }]
}
```

Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-region disaster recovery planning at scale, including SAP replication, AWS DR primitives, and governance. Requires concrete IaC and a runbook-oriented workflow.

Key Concepts
- SAP HANA System Replication (HSR)
- AWS DR primitives: S3 backups, cross-region EBS snapshots, Route 53 failover
- IAM SCP governance across accounts; temporary credentials for DR
- Step Functions orchestration; minimal CDK/CloudFormation snippets

Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CDK-like snippet: DR role and Step Functions skeleton
const drRole = new iam.Role(this, 'SAPDRRole', {
  assumedBy: new iam.AccountPrincipal('DR-ACCOUNT-ID'),
  inlinePolicies: { allow: new iam.PolicyDocument({ statements: [/* perms */] }) }
});

const drStateMachine = new sfn.StateMachine(this, 'SAPDRStateMachine', {
  definition: new sfn.Pass(this, 'Init')
});
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate RPO/RTO during drills without impacting production SAP?
- What metrics and logs would you centralize for audit and post-DR learning?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of patching SAP on AWS using native tools, balancing downtime and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager
- Maintenance windows
- Patch baselines and approvals
- Staging vs production rollout
- Audit trails with CloudTrail and Config
- SAP-specific patch cadence

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "Resources": {
    "SAPPatchRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": {
          "Version": "2012-10-17",
          "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": {"Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com"]}, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ]
        },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [
          "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore",
          "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMFullAccess"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate patch success without SAP downtime impact?
- How would you roll back patches if a patch disrupts SAP services?
